their Meta Platforms copyright headers and BSD-style license; the
TorchTitan license from the pinned dependency eddce126 is included as
LICENSE.torchtitan.
https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan

Local changes connect the public xmixers AutoConfig/AutoModel interface to
independent PISA kernels, preserve PT/CPT target conventions, and add
model/Adam DCP initialization for a new CPT stage. The public Flame training
loop, optional parallelism implementations and tools are retained; PISA
attention currently supports data parallelism only.
